Package: eventscreen
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/RCRaceHub/EventScreenDisplay
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), dbus, avahi-daemon, adduser, network-manager, dnsmasq-base
Recommends: cog, libgles2, libnss-mdns, fonts-dejavu-core
Suggests: cage, seatd, chromium-browser
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Lightweight web page viewer for Raspberry Pi event screens
 Cycles a full-screen kiosk browser through a playlist of web pages, such
 as live RCTC timing boards, on a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W or Pi 3. Controlled
 over a small local HTTP API and advertised on the LAN with mDNS so a
 central manager can find it. Runs unattended and recovers by itself from
 Wi-Fi drops, server restarts and browser crashes. If it can't find a
 known Wi-Fi network it starts a setup hotspot so a phone can pick one.
